micromoog <micromoog@gmail.com> wrote:
> Castle weirdness: when returning from the Valley via the stairs, I
> ended up in a 1x1 room with undiggable walls, almost in the very
> bottom-right corner (two squares south of the southeasternmost floor
> tile).  I had to levelport out.

This also happened to me, not on Spork, but on a NetHack with paxeds
fliplevel patch:

--|     |}| |   |
}}-------}| | --|
 }}}}}}}}}|  <  |
-----------------
                @

This bug appears because returning from the Valley to the Castle is
treated special.

NetHack tries to find a viable place to put you back on the castle in
the right hand side in do.c in the function goto_level on line 1136:

if (Is_stronghold(&u.uz)) {
    register xchar x, y;

    do {
        x = (COLNO - 2 - rnd(5));
        y = rn1(ROWNO - 4, 3);
    } while(occupied(x, y) ||
            IS_WALL(levl[x][y].typ));
    u_on_newpos(x, y);
} else u_on_sstairs();

Now, the selection of x and y is carefully crafted for the layout of
the castle.

But because level flipping can turn it upside down, the first 2 rows
of the castle level which consists of non diggable rocks are at the
bottom and that's where the player might get stuck.

Changing IS_WALL(...) to !SPACE_POS(...) should fix this.


But another "bug" is that the player always gets put on the right side
of the level irregardless on how the level has been flipped. If the
stairs are also on the right side because of the flipping, the player
wouldn't have to cross the castle ever again.

